  "body": "## What\n\nRedesigns the Configure Claude Code page (from v5.7.x) to be more readable and give the connection decision a proper home. The page now opens with a dedicated **\"Choose how you connect\"** section: two flat side-by-side option cards (matching the flat+dense dashboard convention).\n\n### Per session — \"Run `mcc-claude`\"\n- Points only the current shell session at My Claude Code, without touching any file; normal `claude` keeps your standard Anthropic account.\n- Two **copyable command blocks**: `mcc-claude` and `mcc-claude --discover-models` — each with a **Copy** button (reusing the existing `guide-copy-button` pattern).\n- Note that `--discover-models` also lists the gateway models in the `/model` picker.\n\n### Permanent — \"Configure the settings file\"\n- Writes the proxy URL + token into `settings.json` so every Claude Code session points at My Claude Code.\n- Points at the Configure panel below (and the Guide for hand-editing).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Built with `/ui-ux-pro-max` (the skill's command-block + flat+dense guidance; no exact \"two-option comparison\" rule exists in its DB — said so explicitly).\n- Real browser on a throwaway server: both option cards render (badges \"Per session\" / \"Permanent\"), both command blocks show Copy buttons, and clicking Copy flips the button to \"Copied\" (clipboard write succeeded).\n- 126 admin/docs/onboarding tests pass; full suite 3706 passed, 26 known environmental failures (identical baseline), zero new regressions. ruff format/check + ty clean.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Copy buttons rely on `navigator.clipboard` (already used across the dashboard on the localhost origin); the button still leaves the text selectable if clipboard is unavailable.\n- The two-option grid uses `auto-fit minmax(280px, 1fr)`, so on a very narrow viewport the cards stack — intentional, keeps them readable.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
