    "message": "feat(admin): redesign Configure Claude Code page with \"choose how you connect\"\n\nThe Configure Claude Code page now opens with a dedicated \"Choose how you\nconnect\" section: two flat side-by-side option cards (flat + dense, per the\ndashboard convention) that make the decision legible at a glance.\n\n- \"Run mcc-claude\" (Per session): points only the current shell at My Claude\n  Code without touching any file; normal `claude` keeps the Anthropic account.\n  Two copyable command blocks — `mcc-claude` and\n  `mcc-claude --discover-models` — each with a Copy button (reusing the\n  existing guide-copy-button pattern), plus a note that the discover-models\n  flag also lists the gateway models in the /model picker.\n- \"Configure the settings file\" (Permanent): writes the proxy URL + token into\n  settings.json so every session points at My Claude Code; points at the\n  Configure panel below and the Guide for hand-editing.\n\nBuilt with /ui-ux-pro-max (the skill's command-block and flat+dense guidance;\nno exact \"two-option comparison\" rule exists in its DB, said so explicitly).\nVerified in a real browser: both cards render, both command blocks show Copy\nbuttons, and clicking Copy flips the button to \"Copied\" (clipboard write\nsucceeded). Full suite: 3706 passed, 26 known environmental failures, zero new\nregressions. ruff/ty clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
